00:39:34,789 --> 00:39:38,959
<i>‪In other words, regardless of the numbers,</i>

877
00:39:39,043 --> 00:39:42,713
<i>‪any single dot can only have</i>
<i>‪two lines or none extending from it.</i>

878
00:39:42,797 --> 00:39:44,507
<i>‪Identifying such a clear rule</i>

879
00:39:44,590 --> 00:39:48,302
<i>‪to distinguish</i>
<i>‪where lines can and cannot go</i>

880
00:39:48,386 --> 00:39:51,722
<i>‪is the most accurate way</i>
<i>‪to solve this puzzle.</i>

881
00:39:57,770 --> 00:39:59,897
<i>‪I was sure I'd be the fastest.</i>

882
00:40:02,900 --> 00:40:04,777
<i>‪But JAE JAE suddenly pressed the buzzer.</i>

883
00:40:11,784 --> 00:40:12,701
<i>‪JAE JAE.</i>

884
00:40:16,038 --> 00:40:17,206
<i>‪Correct.</i>

885
00:40:18,207 --> 00:40:20,209
‪-Yes!
<i>‪-You have survived.</i>

886
00:40:20,960 --> 00:40:22,545
<i>‪She solved it in no time.</i>

887
00:40:23,129 --> 00:40:25,214
<i>‪I was only about 12 lines in,</i>

888
00:40:25,297 --> 00:40:27,133
<i>‪but she managed to </i><i>‪complete</i>
<i>‪the whole thing.</i>

889
00:40:27,842 --> 00:40:29,135
<i>‪I had to give it to her.</i>

890
00:40:29,218 --> 00:40:30,886
<i>‪I couldn't even come close.</i>

891
00:40:30,970 --> 00:40:33,681
<i>‪JAE JAE managed to </i><i>‪come </i><i>‪in </i><i>‪first</i>
<i>‪two games in a row,</i>

892
00:40:33,764 --> 00:40:36,642
<i>‪so it made me realize</i>
<i>‪how strong a player she was.</i>

893
00:40:37,268 --> 00:40:39,353
<i>‪I was amazed. I realized how good she was.</i>

894
00:40:39,854 --> 00:40:41,272
‪I was so excited.

895
00:40:41,772 --> 00:40:45,317
<i>‪A few easy ones suck you right in,</i>
<i>‪making you connect line after line.</i>

896
00:40:46,068 --> 00:40:49,280
‪You go, "I think I've got this!
‪Oh my gosh, I think I got it!"

897
00:40:49,363 --> 00:40:52,783
<i>‪Then you reach a point</i>
<i>‪where a third of your fence is a mess.</i>

898
00:40:53,367 --> 00:40:55,411
<i>‪The lines just refuse to connect.</i>

899
00:40:56,579 --> 00:41:00,791
‪But you can't give up.
‪You just have to restart.

900
00:41:01,375 --> 00:41:03,085
<i>‪You can't let yourself get stuck there.</i>

901
00:41:03,711 --> 00:41:07,673
<i>‪I kept erasing the parts that didn't work</i>
<i>‪until things started to fall into place.</i>

902
00:41:08,549 --> 00:41:09,925
<i>‪And eventually, I got it right.</i>

903
00:41:13,095 --> 00:41:14,597
‪I'm screwed.

904
00:41:15,222 --> 00:41:17,057
‪ANSWER KEY

905
00:41:17,141 --> 00:41:19,185
<i>‪One wrong move, and it's all over.</i>

906
00:41:21,395 --> 00:41:22,730
‪Do I have to erase everything?

907
00:41:29,278 --> 00:41:30,112
‪Restart.

908
00:41:30,696 --> 00:41:33,491
<i>‪I had to completely restart</i>
<i>‪at least three or four times.</i>

909
00:41:40,623 --> 00:41:42,875
<i>‪Regardless, I still gave it my all.</i>

910
00:42:02,645 --> 00:42:03,771
<i>‪Oh Hyun-min.</i>

911
00:42:07,816 --> 00:42:09,235
<i>‪Correct.</i>

912
00:42:09,318 --> 00:42:10,402
<i>‪You have survived.</i>

913
00:42:12,446 --> 00:42:13,989
<i>‪I expected him to do well.</i>

914
00:42:14,073 --> 00:42:16,158
‪He was quick, as expected.

915
00:42:17,243 --> 00:42:20,996
<i>‪I'm normally not the type</i>
<i>‪to consider second place good enough.</i>

916
00:42:21,622 --> 00:42:25,000
‪But right now, I'm really at peace.

917
00:42:31,131 --> 00:42:34,552
<i>‪I almost gave up at that point.</i>

918
00:42:34,635 --> 00:42:36,554
<i>‪I honestly felt so hopeless.</i>

919
00:42:40,140 --> 00:42:43,102
<i>‪I actually thought I had a shot at this.</i>

920
00:42:43,185 --> 00:42:45,145
<i>‪But when it was just me and Seok-jin left,</i>

921
00:42:45,229 --> 00:42:47,731
<i>‪I realized I might be going home.</i>

922
00:42:48,357 --> 00:42:55,364
‪ANSWER KEY

923
00:43:00,911 --> 00:43:02,246
<i>‪They took a really long time,</i>

924
00:43:02,329 --> 00:43:03,706
<i>‪but I completely understood.</i>

925
00:43:03,789 --> 00:43:06,166
‪Once you lose track of things,
‪it's hard to find your way back.

926
00:43:09,295 --> 00:43:11,880
<i>‪Things started falling into place</i>

927
00:43:12,506 --> 00:43:13,882
<i>‪while taking it step by step.</i>

928
00:43:19,430 --> 00:43:20,973
‪Oh, this will work.

929
00:43:22,057 --> 00:43:25,102
‪Two threes next to each other,
‪so it can only go like this.

930
00:43:26,895 --> 00:43:31,275
<i>‪I realized the key </i><i>‪was </i><i>‪ruling </i><i>‪out</i>
<i>‪what doesn't work.</i>

931
00:44:09,730 --> 00:44:11,190
‪I need to figure out this part.

932
00:44:15,027 --> 00:44:16,362
‪I could do this.

933
00:44:18,280 --> 00:44:19,281
‪Come on.

934
00:44:33,712 --> 00:44:34,880
<i>‪Ha Seok-jin.</i>

935
00:44:37,800 --> 00:44:38,842
<i>‪Correct.</i>

936
00:44:39,551 --> 00:44:40,844
<i>‪You have survived.</i>

937
00:44:41,845 --> 00:44:44,264
<i>‪That concludes the exile zone match.</i>

938
00:44:46,016 --> 00:44:48,435
<i>‪Farewell, Stella Jang.</i>

939
00:44:52,648 --> 00:44:54,650
‪We'll make sure your legacy lives on!

940
00:44:55,234 --> 00:44:56,151
‪You did amazing.

941
00:44:58,320 --> 00:44:59,238
‪Take care.

942
00:44:59,321 --> 00:45:00,322
‪You should be proud.

943
00:45:00,406 --> 00:45:01,407
‪Good job.

944
00:45:01,490 --> 00:45:02,533
‪You did well.

945
00:45:03,575 --> 00:45:04,535
<i>‪I feel relieved.</i>

946
00:45:05,786 --> 00:45:08,664
‪Honestly, I think being in the exile zone
‪made it more fun.

947
00:45:08,747 --> 00:45:11,667
‪I'm a little sad
‪about not seeing the path open up,

948
00:45:12,251 --> 00:45:15,546
<i>‪but I got to solve the puzzle,</i>
<i>‪which </i><i>‪was </i><i>‪like </i><i>‪my </i><i>‪white </i><i>‪whale,</i>

949
00:45:15,629 --> 00:45:20,426
<i>‪and I get to leave the exile zone</i>
<i>‪with everything pretty much solved.</i>

950
00:45:20,509 --> 00:45:22,719
<i>‪So I feel good about that.</i>

951
00:45:23,303 --> 00:45:27,683
‪I think Jin-ho, Nucksal,
‪Yi Do, and Shindong

952
00:45:27,766 --> 00:45:30,436
‪would all agree that I did my part

953
00:45:32,438 --> 00:45:34,731
‪in solving the puzzles.

954
00:45:35,315 --> 00:45:38,318
‪I have no regrets. I had fun.

955
00:45:50,789 --> 00:45:51,874
‪-Good job today.
‪-You too.

956
00:45:51,957 --> 00:45:52,958
‪-You too.
‪-You too.

957
00:45:53,041 --> 00:45:54,168
‪Good job, everyone.

958
00:45:54,793 --> 00:45:55,669
‪You too.

959
00:46:00,632 --> 00:46:02,134
‪Oh man.

960
00:46:02,718 --> 00:46:03,969
‪We've thinned out a lot.

961
00:46:06,972 --> 00:46:09,183
‪It really is tough.

962
00:46:09,266 --> 00:46:10,392
‪It's exhausting.

963
00:46:11,143 --> 00:46:12,269
‪Won-young.

964
00:46:21,737 --> 00:46:22,779
‪Yes?

965
00:46:22,863 --> 00:46:24,198
‪Good job today.

966
00:46:24,865 --> 00:46:28,494
‪-I really fought hard today.
‪-Right.

967
00:46:30,412 --> 00:46:32,915
‪I have some questions.

968
00:46:34,082 --> 00:46:35,667
‪How much of it was real?

969
00:46:36,168 --> 00:46:37,085
‪The token?

970
00:46:37,169 --> 00:46:39,087
‪I'm asking about everything.

971
00:46:41,882 --> 00:46:44,009
‪You said that if you succeeded,

972
00:46:44,092 --> 00:46:46,845
‪-you would earn that thing.
‪-Right.

973
00:46:46,929 --> 00:46:50,641
‪Then why didn't you use it yesterday?

974
00:46:53,101 --> 00:46:56,146
<i>‪Dong-min is still in the dark</i>

975
00:46:56,230 --> 00:46:59,358
<i>‪about how the token is issued</i>
<i>‪and what it actually entails,</i>

976
00:46:59,441 --> 00:47:01,485
‪and I think that's why
‪he's trying to feel me out.

977
00:47:02,319 --> 00:47:03,737
‪But I don't think I'll be sharing.

978
00:47:04,363 --> 00:47:08,575
‪I'm just curious, that's all.
‪You're not obligated to answer.

979
00:47:08,659 --> 00:47:10,160
‪-No.
‪-Right.

980
00:47:10,661 --> 00:47:12,913
‪If you wanna talk,

981
00:47:12,996 --> 00:47:15,499
‪you need to tell me the truth.

982
00:47:15,582 --> 00:47:19,044
‪-If you don't, you just say--
‪-"I'd rather not."

983
00:47:19,127 --> 00:47:21,547
‪-Yeah, I'd be fine with that.
‪-Right.

984
00:47:21,630 --> 00:47:23,757
‪That'd be totally understandable
‪from a strategic standpoint.

985
00:47:23,840 --> 00:47:27,135
<i>‪However, information is power here.</i>

986
00:47:27,219 --> 00:47:28,428
<i>‪That's why…</i>

987
00:47:28,512 --> 00:47:30,430
‪Can I ask you something first?

988
00:47:30,514 --> 00:47:31,473
‪Sure.

989
00:47:32,766 --> 00:47:36,728
‪-You offered Shindong the alliance token
‪-Right.

990
00:47:36,812 --> 00:47:38,188
‪in exchange for information.

991
00:47:38,272 --> 00:47:39,106
‪Yeah.

992
00:47:40,148 --> 00:47:44,528
‪You knew my goal
‪was to make him come in last,

993
00:47:44,611 --> 00:47:46,863
‪-and that would've gotten in the way.
‪-No, that wasn't--

994
00:47:46,947 --> 00:47:49,199
‪So why did you push him up in the ranks?

995
00:47:49,283 --> 00:47:50,867
‪Were you trying to get me eliminated?

996
00:47:50,951 --> 00:47:52,035
‪No, that's not it.

997
00:47:52,786 --> 00:47:53,912
‪Not at all.

998
00:47:53,996 --> 00:47:55,789
‪I told you that day

999
00:47:55,872 --> 00:47:58,834
‪that I wouldn't share that information
‪with anyone,

1000
00:47:58,917 --> 00:48:01,587
‪but it was up to you
‪to work with Shindong.

1001
00:48:01,670 --> 00:48:04,965
‪I promised I wouldn't interfere
‪with your play. You remember, right?

1002
00:48:05,048 --> 00:48:07,676
‪I was giving both of you equal treatment.

1003
00:48:07,759 --> 00:48:10,137
‪If I had wanted to stop you,
‪I would've told Shindong.

1004
00:48:10,220 --> 00:48:11,847
‪"If you do this, you'll come in last."

1005
00:48:11,930 --> 00:48:14,141
‪-If I had wanted to prevent it,
‪-You did keep that promise.

1006
00:48:14,224 --> 00:48:16,393
‪I could've put an end to it all.

1007
00:48:16,476 --> 00:48:18,562
‪I don't know
‪what you're thinking right now,

1008
00:48:18,645 --> 00:48:20,522
‪but is that really the stance
‪you're taking?

1009
00:48:20,606 --> 00:48:23,609
‪You didn't go all out
‪to interfere with me,

1010
00:48:23,692 --> 00:48:27,779
‪but giving Shindong useful information
‪did hinder me a bit.

1011
00:48:27,863 --> 00:48:30,365
‪I did feel targeted at the time.

1012
00:48:30,449 --> 00:48:32,659
‪-I mean, if that's how you felt…
‪-It could be a misunderstanding.

1013
00:48:32,743 --> 00:48:35,621
‪You're free to think that way.

1014
00:48:35,704 --> 00:48:39,833
‪Honestly, I don't believe
‪in permanent allies or enemies.

1015
00:48:39,916 --> 00:48:41,543
‪Today's enemy can be tomorrow's ally.

1016
00:48:41,627 --> 00:48:45,464
‪I just wanted to see
‪if there was anything I could do

1017
00:48:45,547 --> 00:48:48,300
<i>‪to help him relax</i>
<i>‪or make things easier for him.</i>

1018
00:48:48,383 --> 00:48:51,011
<i>‪But that punk started giving me attitude,</i>

1019
00:48:51,094 --> 00:48:52,596
<i>‪so I don't think</i>
<i>‪we'll </i><i>‪be </i><i>‪working </i><i>‪together.</i>

1020
00:48:52,679 --> 00:48:55,766
‪I have zero trust in him.

1021
00:48:59,519 --> 00:49:01,563
‪Hyun-gyu has changed a lot
‪since the first day.

1022
00:49:02,272 --> 00:49:03,357
‪Hyun-gyu?

1023
00:49:03,440 --> 00:49:05,692
‪Most people seem to get there

1024
00:49:05,776 --> 00:49:07,444
‪around this point.

1025
00:49:07,527 --> 00:49:11,281
‪Some forget to take care of themselves,
‪and it catches up with them, like me.

1026
00:49:12,699 --> 00:49:16,036
‪Honestly, staying alive
‪feels meaningless at this point.

1027
00:49:16,119 --> 00:49:18,413
‪I've just been in this prison for days.

1028
00:49:18,914 --> 00:49:20,540
‪Will two people be going home again today?

1029
00:49:20,624 --> 00:49:21,667
‪Isn't that a bit much?

1030
00:49:21,750 --> 00:49:23,627
‪-Maybe…
‪-It might be one today.

1031
00:49:23,710 --> 00:49:26,797
‪I feel like there'll only be
‪one elimination today.

1032
00:49:26,880 --> 00:49:28,590
‪Hold on, that's me.

1033
00:49:29,800 --> 00:49:33,011
‪-It'll all depend on the game.
‪-I'm an OG prison member.

1034
00:49:33,095 --> 00:49:35,013
‪Cut me some slack.

1035
00:49:35,097 --> 00:49:36,431
‪Yeah, you're one of the OGs.

1036
00:49:36,515 --> 00:49:38,809
<i>‪XITSUH is indeed</i>
<i>‪one of the original members.</i>

1037
00:49:38,892 --> 00:49:42,979
‪But on the second day, he switched over
‪to Dong-min's side without hesitation.

1038
00:49:43,063 --> 00:49:44,648
<i>‪After that seamless transition,</i>

1039
00:49:44,731 --> 00:49:46,733
<i>‪he remained dedicated to them even today.</i>

1040
00:49:46,817 --> 00:49:50,904
‪If XITSUH doesn't get eliminated today
‪and returns to the living area tomorrow,

1041
00:49:50,987 --> 00:49:52,864
‪he'll be an enemy once again.

1042
00:49:52,948 --> 00:49:55,867
<i>‪And I don't think there'll be</i>
<i>‪two eliminations today.</i>

1043
00:49:55,951 --> 00:49:59,329
<i>‪I'm thinking it'll be just one,</i>
<i>‪considering </i><i>‪how </i><i>‪the </i><i>‪numbers </i><i>‪are </i><i>‪shrinking.</i>

1044
00:49:59,413 --> 00:50:03,333
‪So starting today, we'll be playing
‪three-on-one to take out one person.

1045
00:50:03,417 --> 00:50:06,086
‪There will be no free-for-all situation
‪like yesterday.

1046
00:50:06,169 --> 00:50:07,921
‪It feels like I'm back at home.

1047
00:50:18,348 --> 00:50:21,393
‪If it's Wall Go,

1048
00:50:21,476 --> 00:50:23,186
‪we isolate XITSUH first.

1049
00:50:23,270 --> 00:50:25,439
‪-Sure.
‪-We can't let him come in first.

1050
00:50:26,022 --> 00:50:29,276
‪We should be at the final one-on-one.
‪That's the way to go.

1051
00:50:29,359 --> 00:50:30,360
‪It won't be Wall Go.

1052
00:50:30,444 --> 00:50:32,320
‪-I'm with you there, but you never know.
‪-Okay.

1053
00:50:33,363 --> 00:50:37,492
‪Either way, if someone needs to go,
‪three-on-one was always our strategy.

1054
00:50:37,576 --> 00:50:39,286
‪We'll help each other out if we can.

1055
00:50:39,369 --> 00:50:41,121
‪That was our goal today.

1056
00:50:41,204 --> 00:50:42,622
‪-Once we take him out,
‪-Right.

1057
00:50:42,706 --> 00:50:44,499
‪their alliance will be down
‪to just Dong-jae.

1058
00:50:47,753 --> 00:50:49,254
‪Goodness.

1059
00:50:51,423 --> 00:50:54,217
‪There really aren't many of us left.
‪Both up there and down here.

1060
00:50:54,301 --> 00:50:55,260
‪Yeah.

1061
00:50:55,844 --> 00:50:57,220
‪I almost forgot.

1062
00:50:57,304 --> 00:50:59,514
‪How many Pieces do you have? None?

1063
00:50:59,598 --> 00:51:00,640
‪-Zero.
‪-Zero, right?

1064
00:51:00,724 --> 00:51:01,641
‪How many do you have?

1065
00:51:02,309 --> 00:51:03,769
‪I have four. Do you want some?

1066
00:51:04,519 --> 00:51:06,605
‪Should we give him one each?
‪Then it'd be three, three, two.

1067
00:51:07,105 --> 00:51:09,191
‪-He couldn't get any because of us.
‪-Right.

1068
00:51:09,274 --> 00:51:11,401
‪I'll give him one Piece.

1069
00:51:12,027 --> 00:51:16,281
<i>‪Sharing Pieces</i>
<i>‪has reinforced the team bond.</i>

1070
00:51:16,364 --> 00:51:20,243
‪And I hoped it might solidify
‪the three-against-one dynamic.

1071
00:51:20,327 --> 00:51:23,163
‪That's why I decided
‪to give him one of my Pieces.

1072
00:51:27,000 --> 00:51:28,543
<i>‪The prison match</i>

1073
00:51:28,627 --> 00:51:30,504
<i>‪will begin in 30 minutes.</i>

1074
00:51:30,587 --> 00:51:34,174
<i>‪In today's prison match,</i>
<i>‪one player will be eliminated</i>

1075
00:51:34,257 --> 00:51:36,426
<i>‪and leave </i>‪The Devil's Plan.

1076
00:51:36,510 --> 00:51:37,511
‪That's a first.

1077
00:51:37,594 --> 00:51:41,348
<i>‪Now, let me introduce</i>
<i>‪the third prison match.</i>

1078
00:51:41,431 --> 00:51:43,266
<i>‪Today's prison match is</i>

1079
00:51:43,350 --> 00:51:44,935
<i>‪Piggy Bank.</i>

1080
00:51:45,519 --> 00:51:46,645
‪Oh, shit.

1081
00:51:46,728 --> 00:51:48,146
‪-What? It's not what I expected.
‪-What?

1082
00:51:48,230 --> 00:51:49,439
<i>‪In Piggy Bank,</i>

1083
00:51:49,523 --> 00:51:53,527
<i>‪players must remember</i>
<i>‪the number of coins inside a piggy bank</i>

1084
00:51:53,610 --> 00:51:55,904
<i>‪and earn points by doubting others.</i>

1085
00:51:55,987 --> 00:51:57,322
‪Is it a memory game?

1086
00:51:57,405 --> 00:51:58,448
<i>‪Before the game begins,</i>

1087
00:51:58,532 --> 00:52:01,785
<i>‪lottery balls will be drawn</i>
