01:12:50,491 --> 01:12:52,951
‪"God's numbers…"

1503
01:12:53,035 --> 01:12:55,662
‪"The sum of God's numbers is zero"?

1504
01:12:55,746 --> 01:12:59,666
‪Maybe the sum of each row
‪of this test is zero.

1505
01:12:59,750 --> 01:13:01,835
‪Does it apply to every row,
‪column, and diagonal?

1506
01:13:02,586 --> 01:13:07,257
‪"The sum of horizontal numbers
‪of the test equals zero."

1507
01:13:07,341 --> 01:13:10,135
‪"The sum of vertical numbers equals zero."

1508
01:13:10,219 --> 01:13:12,679
‪"The sum of diagonal numbers."

1509
01:13:13,472 --> 01:13:14,890
‪That's where it ends.

1510
01:13:14,973 --> 01:13:17,059
‪We concluded they're all equal.

1511
01:13:17,142 --> 01:13:18,685
‪All three sums are equal.

1512
01:13:19,269 --> 01:13:20,979
‪-The sums of each row, column,
‪-Makes sense.

1513
01:13:21,063 --> 01:13:22,189
‪and diagonal are all equal.

1514
01:13:23,190 --> 01:13:24,066
‪Isn't that a magic square?

1515
01:13:24,149 --> 01:13:26,693
‪-That's what I thought.
‪-Right.

1516
01:13:27,277 --> 01:13:29,113
‪Hyun-min, you're really good.

1517
01:13:29,655 --> 01:13:33,158
‪Is number one fixed in this position
‪on this seven-by-seven board?

1518
01:13:33,242 --> 01:13:34,159
‪We think so.

1519
01:13:35,119 --> 01:13:37,704
‪A magic square without a fixed number
‪should always be solvable.

1520
01:13:37,788 --> 01:13:39,248
‪There's a magic square
‪without a fixed number?

1521
01:13:39,331 --> 01:13:41,250
‪If I can place number one wherever I want,

1522
01:13:41,333 --> 01:13:42,876
‪I can definitely solve it.

1523
01:13:42,960 --> 01:13:44,336
‪We managed to solve it.

1524
01:13:44,420 --> 01:13:46,922
‪-You made a seven-by-seven magic square?
‪-Yeah, we did.

1525
01:13:47,005 --> 01:13:48,298
‪Using 1 through 49?

1526
01:13:48,382 --> 01:13:50,676
‪No, just one to seven.

1527
01:13:50,759 --> 01:13:52,970
‪You mean, you used one through seven,
‪seven times, right?

1528
01:13:53,053 --> 01:13:54,012
‪Right.

1529
01:13:54,096 --> 01:13:55,639
‪That's completely different.

1530
01:13:55,722 --> 01:13:56,849
‪Using one to seven, and using--

1531
01:13:56,932 --> 01:13:58,559
‪Their numbers only go up to nine.

1532
01:13:58,642 --> 01:14:01,520
‪-Yeah, it probably won't go up to 49.
‪-You can combine the numbers though.

1533
01:14:01,603 --> 01:14:02,729
‪That's true.

1534
01:14:02,813 --> 01:14:04,189
‪You can combine the numbers
‪to make double digits.

1535
01:14:04,273 --> 01:14:06,066
‪Didn't we see numbers

1536
01:14:06,150 --> 01:14:08,026
‪that were written together
‪to make double digits?

1537
01:14:08,110 --> 01:14:09,862
‪-Isn't there 60 somewhere?
‪-Yeah, there is.

1538
01:14:09,945 --> 01:14:11,989
‪-It was 60 minutes.
‪-Yeah. 60 minutes and 365 days.

1539
01:14:12,072 --> 01:14:14,491
‪-I think you can combine them here.
‪-Really?

1540
01:14:14,575 --> 01:14:16,452
‪I mean, 365 exists.

1541
01:14:16,535 --> 01:14:18,495
<i>‪Hyun-min immediately figured out</i>
<i>‪it was a magic square.</i>

1542
01:14:18,579 --> 01:14:21,039
‪But he said that on top of the version
‪using numbers one to seven,

1543
01:14:21,123 --> 01:14:23,459
‪there's another one
‪that uses numbers 1 to 49.

1544
01:14:23,542 --> 01:14:25,461
<i>‪I only learned about it then.</i>

1545
01:14:25,961 --> 01:14:28,005
‪-Can only one person attempt it?
‪-Yeah, only one person.

1546
01:14:28,088 --> 01:14:29,339
‪-Only one.
‪-Okay.

1547
01:14:29,423 --> 01:14:31,550
‪But if they fail, someone else can try.

1548
01:14:32,134 --> 01:14:33,760
‪-Oh, they can?
‪-On the same day?

1549
01:14:33,844 --> 01:14:34,678
‪That, we don't know.

1550
01:14:34,761 --> 01:14:36,305
‪Probably the next day.

1551
01:14:36,889 --> 01:14:38,682
‪I don't think it'll be so hard to crack.

1552
01:14:38,765 --> 01:14:43,937
‪Right, so we're arming ourselves
‪with everything we can

1553
01:14:44,021 --> 01:14:45,689
‪-and waiting for tomorrow morning.
‪-Okay.

1554
01:14:45,772 --> 01:14:48,108
‪We'll try blocking that
‪when the bird calls out.

1555
01:14:48,192 --> 01:14:49,776
‪Does it cover the eye perfectly?

1556
01:14:49,860 --> 01:14:51,778
‪-Yeah, we tried it once.
‪-Pretty much.

1557
01:14:51,862 --> 01:14:53,780
‪It doesn't do anything now,
‪but it does fit.

1558
01:14:53,864 --> 01:14:54,740
‪Do you wanna try?

1559
01:14:55,365 --> 01:14:56,700
‪-You can try holding it up.
‪-I also…

1560
01:14:56,783 --> 01:14:58,452
‪-Try holding it.
‪-I am curious, actually.

1561
01:14:58,535 --> 01:14:59,536
‪Here.

1562
01:15:01,079 --> 01:15:03,499
‪We're thinking something might happen

1563
01:15:04,082 --> 01:15:05,542
‪if we cover it when the bird calls out.

1564
01:15:06,710 --> 01:15:08,378
‪-I'm suddenly in a good mood.
‪-Isn't it fun?

1565
01:15:08,462 --> 01:15:09,796
‪-More so than that,
‪-Yeah?

1566
01:15:09,880 --> 01:15:12,132
‪I'm excited that I can attempt it
‪sooner than I thought.

1567
01:15:12,216 --> 01:15:13,759
‪It might not be that soon.

1568
01:15:13,842 --> 01:15:15,636
‪-But tomorrow--
‪-It's one person per day.

1569
01:15:15,719 --> 01:15:16,845
‪You need to go through

1570
01:15:16,929 --> 01:15:18,931
‪two more exile zone matches
‪before you can take your turn.

1571
01:15:19,014 --> 01:15:20,891
‪You're third in line.

1572
01:15:21,600 --> 01:15:23,560
<i>‪I really wanna take on </i><i>‪the </i><i>‪challenge</i>
<i>‪tomorrow </i><i>‪morning.</i>

1573
01:15:23,644 --> 01:15:25,062
‪But I'm not speaking up

1574
01:15:25,145 --> 01:15:27,773
‪because Seok-jin is the one
‪who first mentioned the magic square

1575
01:15:27,856 --> 01:15:29,399
‪and solved it.

1576
01:15:29,483 --> 01:15:31,818
‪So I'll quietly wait for my turn.

1577
01:15:31,902 --> 01:15:35,322
‪Even though it's a solution
‪for one possible form of a game,

1578
01:15:35,405 --> 01:15:37,699
<i>‪I did work it out in advance,</i>

1579
01:15:37,783 --> 01:15:41,537
‪and because of that,
‪she implied that I should go first.

1580
01:15:41,620 --> 01:15:43,664
‪So when the bird calls out tomorrow,

1581
01:15:43,747 --> 01:15:45,999
‪I'll try holding up the moon.

1582
01:15:46,583 --> 01:15:47,960
‪Tomorrow is the fourth day.

1583
01:15:48,585 --> 01:15:52,798
‪-Wow, you're right.
‪-If we're going in order,

1584
01:15:52,881 --> 01:15:55,050
‪-Yeah?
‪-we can get three chances max.

1585
01:15:55,133 --> 01:15:56,510
‪If it's one person per day.

1586
01:15:56,593 --> 01:15:59,805
‪Right, but that's assuming Seok-jin fails.

1587
01:15:59,888 --> 01:16:02,516
‪-Right, if he succeeds, that's it.
‪-Then it's over for us.

1588
01:16:04,184 --> 01:16:05,060
‪This is tough.

1589
01:16:05,936 --> 01:16:07,563
<i>‪There's a hierarchy to everything.</i>

1590
01:16:07,646 --> 01:16:09,439
‪I just have to follow the rules here.

1591
01:16:10,023 --> 01:16:12,150
‪But the problem is, if I wait for my turn,
‪it'll be the sixth day.

1592
01:16:12,985 --> 01:16:13,819
‪That's ridiculous.

1593
01:16:13,902 --> 01:16:17,197
‪I know this is terrible of me,

1594
01:16:18,073 --> 01:16:21,660
‪but I've gone so far as to hope
‪that JAE JAE gets eliminated tomorrow.

1595
01:16:22,619 --> 01:16:24,746
‪I just want my chance
‪to come a day sooner.

1596
01:16:25,872 --> 01:16:29,209
‪And honestly, I already know
‪the full magic square solution.

1597
01:16:29,293 --> 01:16:32,045
‪But if someone in front of me succeeds,
‪I don't even get to try.

1598
01:16:32,629 --> 01:16:33,880
‪So I can't get myself to share it.

1599
01:16:34,715 --> 01:16:36,925
‪If I just had paper and a pen…

1600
01:16:37,009 --> 01:16:39,469
‪-I know. We've had the same thought.
‪-I know, right?

1601
01:16:39,553 --> 01:16:40,512
‪The exact same thought.

1602
01:16:41,013 --> 01:16:43,890
‪I didn't know there was a version
‪where you use 1 to 49.

1603
01:16:43,974 --> 01:16:46,602
‪I'd love to see Hyun-min
‪solve it with a formula.

1604
01:16:46,685 --> 01:16:47,728
‪Yeah.

1605
01:16:47,811 --> 01:16:49,605
‪The number one was fixed.

1606
01:16:49,688 --> 01:16:52,899
<i>‪But the solution I have</i>

1607
01:16:52,983 --> 01:16:55,027
‪doesn't have that number there.

1608
01:16:55,110 --> 01:16:58,363
‪If only the starting position
‪weren't fixed,

1609
01:16:59,114 --> 01:17:00,532
‪-I could make it work.
‪-Right.

1610
01:17:00,616 --> 01:17:03,577
‪-Having a set starting point is a blow.
‪-I think it's fixed.

1611
01:17:03,660 --> 01:17:05,370
‪-That must be why they put one here.
‪-Right.

1612
01:17:05,454 --> 01:17:07,456
‪That makes things harder.

1613
01:17:07,539 --> 01:17:08,749
‪-Really?
‪-Yeah.

1614
01:17:08,832 --> 01:17:12,044
‪Would my algorithm work
‪with or without the starting point?

1615
01:17:12,127 --> 01:17:14,588
‪That's what I wanna check, but I can't.

1616
01:17:15,756 --> 01:17:18,550
‪I can't remember how long after sunrise
‪the bird called out.

1617
01:17:18,634 --> 01:17:20,552
‪-Right.
‪-Have you heard it before?

1618
01:17:20,636 --> 01:17:23,013
‪-Yeah, it's really bizarre.
‪-It's loud enough for all to hear.

1619
01:17:23,096 --> 01:17:25,349
‪-Like the screech of a prehistoric bird.
‪-Yeah, that's right.

1620
01:17:25,432 --> 01:17:27,559
‪-And it cries out six times?
‪-Yeah, six times.

1621
01:17:27,643 --> 01:17:29,936
‪We just need to lift it
‪when it starts crying out.

1622
01:17:30,020 --> 01:17:31,355
‪But you can't if you don't wake up.

1623
01:17:32,105 --> 01:17:33,065
‪Damn it.

1624
01:17:33,565 --> 01:17:35,692
‪What if I can't go to sleep
‪because of that?

1625
01:17:35,776 --> 01:17:37,944
‪If you're still sleeping,

1626
01:17:38,028 --> 01:17:39,237
‪-could we possibly--
‪-Wake me up!

1627
01:17:41,531 --> 01:17:43,408
‪I'm gonna hold onto this while sleeping.

1628
01:17:43,492 --> 01:17:44,409
‪We'll splash water on you.

1629
01:17:44,493 --> 01:17:46,244
‪-I'm gonna hold onto it.
‪-I'm asking just in case.

1630
01:17:46,328 --> 01:17:48,413
‪If I don't wake up after all that,
‪then go ahead.

1631
01:17:51,583 --> 01:17:54,378
‪I'm dying to know
‪what time it is right now.

1632
01:17:54,461 --> 01:17:55,420
‪What time is it?

1633
01:17:57,089 --> 01:17:59,091
‪I wish they'd give us paper and a pen.

1634
01:18:00,300 --> 01:18:01,551
‪This is a timeless place.

1635
01:18:02,844 --> 01:18:05,597
‪"This place is neither life nor death."

1636
01:18:31,498 --> 01:18:33,667
‪What were you practicing with?

1637
01:18:33,750 --> 01:18:35,293
‪The little bits from the pillow.

1638
01:18:35,377 --> 01:18:38,004
‪I totally forgot we had buckwheat pillows.

1639
01:18:38,088 --> 01:18:39,464
<i>‪Thinking outside the box again.</i>

1640
01:18:39,548 --> 01:18:41,717
‪He pulled the buckwheat out of the pillow.

1641
01:18:43,051 --> 01:18:46,179
‪Must you make us go this far?

1642
01:18:46,263 --> 01:18:48,849
<i>‪Imagine how flat and uncomfortable</i>
<i>‪his </i><i>‪pillow </i><i>‪must </i><i>‪be </i><i>‪now.</i>

1643
01:18:48,932 --> 01:18:49,891
‪But you know,

1644
01:18:50,517 --> 01:18:52,853
‪-they're really hard to pick up.
‪-Right.

1645
01:18:52,936 --> 01:18:53,854
‪It's pointless.

1646
01:18:56,606 --> 01:18:58,525
‪Is no one coming?

1647
01:18:58,608 --> 01:18:59,943
‪That's impossible.

1648
01:19:00,026 --> 01:19:01,319
‪Surely, someone will come.

1649
01:19:01,403 --> 01:19:03,822
‪-Maybe they chose the blue door.
‪-Oh.

1650
01:19:04,448 --> 01:19:05,365
‪Maybe they did.

1651
01:19:05,449 --> 01:19:07,743
‪I guess they really could've.

1652
01:19:07,826 --> 01:19:08,910
‪Yeah, that makes sense.

1653
01:19:08,994 --> 01:19:11,747
‪I guess they really walked out that door.

1654
01:19:11,830 --> 01:19:13,165
‪Yeah? So, can we just sleep now?

1655
01:19:14,291 --> 01:19:15,125
‪I guess so.

1656
01:19:15,208 --> 01:19:16,042
‪Unbelievable.

1657
01:19:20,672 --> 01:19:23,341
‪I'll wait for that door
‪to open in the morning.

1658
01:19:23,425 --> 01:19:24,801
‪I meant the path.

1659
01:19:24,885 --> 01:19:26,970
‪I'll just watch Seok-jin open that
‪in the morning.

1660
01:19:27,888 --> 01:19:28,930
‪Good night.

1661
01:19:29,014 --> 01:19:29,931
‪Good night.

1662
01:19:30,849 --> 01:19:33,310
‪-Sweet dreams.
‪-Sweet dreams.

1663
01:19:46,114 --> 01:19:47,240
‪It's time!

1664
01:19:47,324 --> 01:19:48,617
‪The bird's gonna call out soon.

1665
01:19:48,700 --> 01:19:49,618
‪It's time.

1666
01:19:49,701 --> 01:19:50,952
<i>‪We can finally</i>

1667
01:19:51,745 --> 01:19:53,455
‪cover the sun today.

1668
01:19:54,206 --> 01:19:57,751
‪Let me flip this first just in case.
‪It's the 15-minute one.

1669
01:20:01,046 --> 01:20:02,422
‪If I get eliminated,

1670
01:20:04,049 --> 01:20:05,425
‪you two should practice this.

1671
01:20:05,509 --> 01:20:07,219
‪But with which option?

1672
01:20:07,302 --> 01:20:08,845
‪I'd go for 49.

1673
01:20:08,929 --> 01:20:11,723
‪If the logic holds, it holds.

1674
01:20:11,807 --> 01:20:13,141
‪Logically, it all works out.

1675
01:20:13,225 --> 01:20:14,559
‪Is it all in your head?

1676
01:20:14,643 --> 01:20:17,270
‪I can do it if I can place the numbers
‪where I want.

1677
01:20:17,354 --> 01:20:19,022
‪But starting from this specific position?

1678
01:20:19,105 --> 01:20:21,358
‪I haven't figured that out yet.

1679
01:20:21,441 --> 01:20:22,651
‪I'll keep working on it.

1680
01:20:23,193 --> 01:20:25,779
<i>‪I was worried about the game</i>
<i>‪being the 1-to-49 version,</i>

1681
01:20:25,862 --> 01:20:28,448
‪but I already figured out
‪the one-to-seven version.

1682
01:20:28,532 --> 01:20:30,534
‪Numbers are just patterns
‪at the end of the day.

1683
01:20:30,617 --> 01:20:35,413
‪I felt that I could find a combination
‪balanced in all directions.

1684
01:20:35,497 --> 01:20:38,708
‪I had this groundless faith in myself.

1685
01:20:38,792 --> 01:20:40,544
‪Fifteen minutes is almost up.

1686
01:20:40,627 --> 01:20:41,503
‪It's almost time.

1687
01:20:41,586 --> 01:20:43,964
‪-Must be 30 minutes then.
‪-Oh, maybe.

1688
01:20:44,047 --> 01:20:45,298
‪It needs to run twice.

1689
01:20:45,382 --> 01:20:46,925
‪I've flipped it again.

1690
01:20:47,008 --> 01:20:48,510
‪It must be 30 minutes.

1691
01:20:52,347 --> 01:20:53,974
‪This bird wakes up really late.

1692
01:20:55,433 --> 01:20:57,018
‪-It went out for drinks last night.
‪-Right.

1693
01:20:57,561 --> 01:20:59,521
‪It's not the most diligent one.

1694
01:20:59,604 --> 01:21:01,022
‪The curiosity is killing me.

1695
01:21:01,106 --> 01:21:03,066
‪What could "day turns to night" mean?

1696
01:21:03,149 --> 01:21:05,193
‪I'm a hyper-inquisitive type,

1697
01:21:05,277 --> 01:21:08,822
‪so I was dying to know what the path
‪and the puzzle would look like.

1698
01:21:08,905 --> 01:21:12,951
‪I think it could be just about this level.

1699
01:21:13,034 --> 01:21:15,078
‪When they designed this,

1700
01:21:15,161 --> 01:21:17,330
‪-Right, they probably…
‪-they might not have expected

1701
01:21:17,414 --> 01:21:20,584
‪people to decode everything
‪and figure all this out together.

1702
01:21:20,667 --> 01:21:23,003
‪So if one person had to decode everything,

1703
01:21:23,086 --> 01:21:25,297
‪solve the other puzzles,

1704
01:21:25,380 --> 01:21:29,384
‪and even work out this game mentally,
‪that'd be an incredible achievement.

1705
01:21:29,467 --> 01:21:31,261
‪Wait, 15 minutes is almost up.

1706
01:21:35,849 --> 01:21:37,350
‪-I hear the bird.
‪-It's the bird!

1707
01:21:38,435 --> 01:21:39,311
‪It's coming.

1708
01:21:51,197 --> 01:21:52,449
‪-It's here!
‪-Cover it!

1709
01:21:52,532 --> 01:21:53,950
‪-Great.
‪-On the sixth call, right?

1710
01:21:54,034 --> 01:21:54,868
‪Yes, that's right.

1711
01:21:54,951 --> 01:21:55,952
‪Right on the sixth call?

1712
01:21:56,036 --> 01:21:57,996
‪Yeah. That was the second call.

1713
01:22:00,707 --> 01:22:01,625
‪-Three.
‪-Three.

1714
01:22:01,708 --> 01:22:02,876
‪No.

1715
01:22:05,629 --> 01:22:06,546
‪-Four.
‪-Four.

1716
01:22:13,178 --> 01:22:14,012
‪Five.

1717
01:22:14,095 --> 01:22:15,221
‪No!

1718
01:22:20,060 --> 01:22:21,353
‪Six!

1719
01:22:21,436 --> 01:22:23,063
‪"When the bird calls out six times,

1720
01:22:23,146 --> 01:22:25,398
‪you cover the sun."

1721
01:22:25,482 --> 01:22:26,608
‪I covered it!

1722
01:22:30,153 --> 01:22:31,112
‪I covered it!

1723
01:22:32,113 --> 01:22:32,948
‪Something's happening.

1724
01:22:34,199 --> 01:22:35,033
‪Something's happening.

1725
01:22:35,116 --> 01:22:36,034
‪Wow! No way!

1726
01:22:36,117 --> 01:22:37,202
‪-Amazing!
‪-I'm getting chills!

1727
01:22:37,285 --> 01:22:38,286
‪No way.

1728
01:22:48,546 --> 01:22:49,381
‪Unbelievable.

1729
